  "id": "director",
  "term": "director",
  "definition": "In this framework, a director is the person on the production side who organizes scene design choices in film or television to shape the viewer’s unfolding expectations, arousal, and emotional response. The director does this by combining formal elements such as camera use, framing, editing, lighting, sound, and cueing to guide a target emotional trajectory.",
